# Web Backend Rules

## Layer separation

- `server.py` — HTTP routing/static serve only
- `service.py` — resolve/download API, encode option mapping
- `jobs.py` — background download workers, worker limits
- `job_store.py` — job persistence; preserve migration paths
- `progress_phase.py` — log line → UI phase labels
- `cleanup.py` — temp file cleanup (`jav-remux-*`, `jav-encode-*`)

## Encode options flow

API JSON fields → `_encode_options_from_mapping()` in `service.py` → `M3U8Crawler.__init__` → `media_post.apply_encode_options()` → `site._encode_*` runtime attrs.

Keep `GET /api/encoding/capabilities` in sync with `encoding_capabilities.py`.

## Static assets

Production UI served from `src/jav_downloader/web/static/`.
Source lives in `web/frontend/` — rebuild with `make web-build`, never hand-edit bundled assets.

## Termux / bind

- `make start` sets `WEB_HOST=0.0.0.0` when `TERMUX_VERSION` is set
- Default `DOWNLOAD_DIR=~/storage/downloads` on Termux

## Tests

- `test_web.py`, `test_web_service.py`, `test_job_store.py`, `test_web_cleanup.py`, `test_progress_phase.py`
